        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "The vertices of \\(\\triangle ABC\\) are \\(A(1,2)\\), \\(B(7,2)\\), and \\(C(4,8)\\). If the medians intersect at \\(G\\), which statement is correct?",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The centroid is \\(G=\\left(\\frac{1+7+4}{3},\\frac{2+2+8}{3}\\right)=(4,4)\\). The proposition on medians states that the centroid divides every median internally in the ratio \\(2:1\\), measured from the vertex.",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
        "points": 10,
        "sort_order": 112,
        "question_data": {
